      "license": "CC0",
      "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en",
      "artist": "Khobbyyyy",
      "description": "The male slave dungeon at Fort Prinzenstein is a dark, cramped, and poorly ventilated underground chamber. The walls are made of thick stone or mud, with minimal lighting, creating an eerie atmosphere. The air is stale, and the conditions are harsh, reflecting the inhumane treatment of enslaved people.\nThe dungeon's small size and lack of amenities highlight the brutal conditions faced by enslaved men, who were often chained and held captive before being transported to the Americas. The fort's history serves as a poignant reminder of the transatlantic slave trade's impact.",
